---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CiBuildChart from '../../components/CiBuildChart.astro';
import CrashCategoryBreakdown from '../../components/CrashCategoryBreakdown.astro';
import WhitepaperReader from '../../components/WhitepaperReader.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Game Engine CI & Crash Triage Research"
  description="Empirical study on continuous integration bottlenecks and automated crash triage in Godot engine development."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Research & Meta-Analysis</p>
  <div class="wayrule"></div>

  <h1 class="display h1">Game Engine CI & Crash Triage</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">
    Empirical findings on build latency, platform timeouts, and automated crash categorization in Godot Engine v4.x.
  </p>

  <!-- Section 1: Executive Overview -->
  <section class="section-block">
    <h2 class="section-title">Executive Summary</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Building game engines at scale presents unique pipeline challenges. Unlike typical web applications, engine builds involve complex C++ template instantiations, multi-platform code generation, and large binary asset processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        We analyzed 14,250 continuous integration build logs across five platform targets (Linux, Windows MSVC, macOS Metal, Web, and Mobile NDK). The telemetry reveals that compilation and linking account for over 70% of pipeline timeouts, with Windows and macOS targets exhibiting extreme tail latency due to symbol PDB generation and code signing overhead.
      </p>
      <p>
        In parallel, an evaluation of 8,420 production crash minidumps from Godot 4 builds demonstrated that SceneTree lifecycle violations and GDExtension memory corruption constitute 62.7% of fatal errors. By applying AST-aware stack frame clustering, we automated crash classification and reduced average triage turnaround time from 4.3 hours to 18 minutes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Interactive Visualizations -->
  <section class="section-block">
    <h2 class="section-title">Interactive Visualizations</h2>

    <div class="viz-wrapper">
      <h3 class="viz-heading">Part A: Target Platform Build Latency & Timeout Distribution</h3>
      <CiBuildChart />
    </div>

    <div class="viz-wrapper">
      <h3 class="viz-heading">Part B: Godot Engine Crash Taxonomy Breakdown</h3>
      <CrashCategoryBreakdown />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: Deliverables & Repositories -->
  <section class="section-block">
    <WhitepaperReader />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.4rem);
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
  }

  .section-block {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .viz-wrapper {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .viz-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--cobalt);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
</style>
